<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr CPI 19.5 pct in Sept vs 20.5 Aug.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr CPI 19.5 pct in Sept vs 20.5 Aug.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 1.9 percent in September against a 0.5 percent rise in August, bringing year-on-year inflation down to 19.5 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>CPI rose 14.0 percent in the January-September period, compared with a 16.3 percent rise in the same period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES	SEPTEMBER   AUGUST    SEPT 1995</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	 1.9	  0.5	  3.0</p>
<p> yr/yr change			19.5	 20.5	 24.2</p>
<p> services m/m change		1.3	  0.7	  1.5</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	   18.9	 19.2	 26.0</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	   2.7	 -0.2	  3.9</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change	20.2	 21.0	 19.9</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
